  "chapter": {
    "number": 39,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(40) For the end, a Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I waited patiently for the Lord; and he attended to me, and listened to my supplication.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he brought me up out of a pit of misery, and from miry clay: and he set my feet on a rock, and ordered my goings aright.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he put a new song into my mouth, even a hymn to our God: many shall see it, and fear, and shall hope in the Lord.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blessed is the man whose hope is in the name of the Lord, and who has not regarded vanities and false frenzies.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord my God, you have multiplied your wonderful works, and in your thoughts there is none who shall be likened to you: I declared and spoke of them: they exceeded number.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Sacrifice and offering you would not; but a body have you prepared me: whole burnt offering and sacrifice for sin you did not require.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Then I said, Behold, I",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 76
          },
          {
            "text": "come: in the volume of the book it is written concerning me,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I desired to do your will, O my God, and your law in the midst of my heart.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I have preached righteousness in the great congregation; behold! I will not refrain my lips; O Lord, you know my righteousness.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I have not hid your truth within my heart, and I have declared your salvation; I have not hid your mercy and your truth from the great congregation.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But you, Lord, remove not your compassion far from me; your mercy and your truth have helped me continually.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For innumerable evils have encompassed me; my transgressions have taken hold of me, and I could not see; they are multiplied more than the hairs of my head; and my heart has failed me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Be pleased, O Lord, to deliver me; O Lord, draw near to help me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let those that seek my soul, to destroy it, be ashamed and confounded together; let those that wish me evil be turned backward and put to shame.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let those that say to me, Aha, aha, quickly receive shame for their reward.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let all those that seek you, O Lord, exult and rejoice in you; and let them that love your salvation say continually, The Lord be magnified.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But I am poor and needy; the Lord will take care of me; you are my helper, and my defender, O my God, delay not.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 76,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, am come.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 39,
          "verse": 7
        }
      }
    ]
  },
